            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123093093?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">MDN's text fragment URL example contains an unencoded colon and I've replaced it by encoding it as %3A</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">MDN's example works even without my fix, but it's just strictly more correct to encode : as %3A. A strict encoder caught this so I thought it worth flagging at least</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
